The probe confirmed that `ACTION3` moves the avatar exactly five cells left while preserving its orientation. The other two changed cells were only the budget bar, which loses one column per movement. I’ll use two confirmed left moves, then test presumed `ACTION1 = up` twice, stopping immediately below the unknown object.

